1082:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *
1083:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  The advantage of function objects over pointers to functions is that
1084:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  the objects in the standard library declare nested typedefs describing
1085:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  their argument and result types with uniform names (e.g., `result_type`
1086:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  from the base classes `unary_function` and `binary_function`).
1087:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  Sometimes those typedefs are required, not just optional.
1088:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *
1089:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  Adaptors are provided to turn pointers to unary (single-argument) and
1090:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  binary (double-argument) functions into function objects.  The
1091:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  long-winded functor `pointer_to_unary_function` is constructed with a
1092:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  function pointer `f`, and its `operator()` called with argument `x`
1093:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  returns `f(x)`.  The functor `pointer_to_binary_function` does the same
1094:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  thing, but with a double-argument `f` and `operator()`.
1095:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *
1096:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  The function `ptr_fun` takes a pointer-to-function `f` and constructs
1097:D:/Program Files/msys64/mingw64/arm-none-eabi/include/c++/13.3.0/bits\stl_function.h ****    *  an instance of the appropriate functor.
